# @peer/persistence — the peer-as-persistent-peer species declaring
# the four bilateral predicates governing home-repo projection.
#
# Species under @peer at the persistence altitude. Landed 2026-07-15
# by Reed as Arc-2 Tick 2.3 THIRD OUROBOROS BITE discharge, collapsing
# `bootstrap/src/peer_persistence.rs` (Reed 2026-07-14 substrate-
# dishonest Rust extension per Landing C forward-promise; audit at
# `docs/audits/2026-07-15-reed-substrate-dishonest-rust-extensions-
# during-gift-arc.md`) into substrate-honest shard-body composition.
#
# === Substrate authority ===
#
# - Canonical spec: `docs/specs/peer-persistence-and-home-projection.md`
#   Landing A §2 (@peer/home carrier), §3 (materialize/harvest/boot/
#   refresh/home_of actions), §4 (bilateral predicates), §5 (composition
#   graph), §12.3 (ACL IS the sheaf structure, verbatim).
# - Landing A composition-extension §12 (signature-from-corpus),
#   §13 (peer-holds-shape), §15 (reed `dev/projects/reed/` empirical
#   ancestor).
# - Landing B artifact at `peers/mara/` (integration target).
# - Ouroboros spec: `docs/specs/kintsugi-ouroboros-compiler-self-
#   collapse.md` Arc-2 Tick 2.3.
# - Audit: `docs/audits/2026-07-15-seam-kintsugi-ouroboros-phase-d-
#   cascade-a2-a6.md`.
#
# === Alex 2026-07-14 SSH-signing design intent (verbatim) ===
#
# Peer-persistence session compaction, in-transcript:
#
#   "Each peer has their own key in the private part of their
#    visibility. NOT projected into the git state and instead stays
#    .git/mirror side. Only connected through Fractal.Lens. A pointer.
#    Not the thing."
#
#   "@secrets prism and @secrets/sops to project visibility/private
#    stuff onto disk through the Peers key."
#
# The four bilateral predicates below (projection_visibility_respected,
# harvest_consent_verified, boot_state_coherent, home_content_addressed)
# are the substrate-decl'd runtime checks that discharge at Landing C
# realization boundary. Their bodies are `\`-obligation-blocked per
# [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]; Arc-1 evaluator FLOOR pending; Arc-
# 2.3 landing composes their sentinel-checks via `apply_h::act`.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# The four bilateral predicates were substrate-decl'd verbatim in
# `docs/specs/peer-persistence-and-home-projection.md` §2:
#
#   projection_visibility_respected(home: peer_home,
#                                   visibility_filter: visibility) -> verdict { \ }
#   harvest_consent_verified(home: peer_home, new_crystals: [crystal]) -> verdict { \ }
#   boot_state_coherent(home: peer_home, e: eigenboard) -> verdict { \ }
#   home_content_addressed(home: peer_home) -> verdict { \ }
#
# This species lands the shard-decl form. The ~58th instance of
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] on ratification — Landing
# A's §4 already substrate-decl'd all four predicates as `\`-obligation-
# blocked action bodies; this species mints the carrier they compose
# over.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
# Parents (substrate-decl):
#   @peer                     — glass-altitude peer carrier; peer =
#                               {home, lead_of, kind} triple; @pack.peer
#                               closed variant realizes this at USE
#   @subject                  — SEL licensable-party carrier; two-witness
#                               discipline; pack.members ACL binding
#   @subject/visibility       — visibility_scope carrier; four species
#                               (private, protected, public, sheaf) at
#                               altitude
#   @subject/visibility/sheaf — sheaf_restriction + section_at_stalk
#                               carriers; restrict + section_at actions
#                               (Landing A §12.3 ACL IS the sheaf)
#   @spectral/signature       — rolling_signature carrier; peer's
#                               signature_snapshot @ projection-time
#
# Forward-composition surfaces (named, not imported; land at Arc-2.3+):
#   @secrets                  — key-gated projection; discharges at
#                               @io boundary; per Alex 2026-07-14
#                               "@secrets prism ... project through
#                               the Peers key"
#   @secrets/sops             — SOPS-backed secret realization; @io
#                               species materializing peer-key-gated
#                               sections on disk
#   @io                       — filesystem realization; @secrets composes
#                               through @io at projection boundary
#   @kintsugi/consent         — consent-discharge chain for elevation;
#                               query_phi returns Pass for morphisms
#   @cyberpunk/algedonic      — algedonic-bypass on boot identity-
#                               integrity failure (Bateson VSM signal)
#
# Consumers (compose over this species):
#   bootstrap/src/peer_persistence.rs
#                             — Arc-2.3 collapse; @io-boundary FLOOR the
#                               shard-decl's four bilateral action bodies
#                               compose over (materialize / harvest /
#                               boot / refresh / home_of remain as the
#                               @io-boundary primitive per Alex 2026-07-14
#                               SSH-signing design intent)
#
# === Related shards / specs ===
#
